 Dong Q, Tan L, Yu JT, et al. Associations of anxiety with amyloid, tau, and neurodegeneration in older adults without dementia: a longitudinal study. J Alzheimers Dis. 2021;82:273–83. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 73. Tissot C, Therriault J, Pascoal TA, Chamoun M, Lussier FZ, Savard M, et al. Association between regional tau pathology and neuropsychiatric symptoms in aging and dementia due to Alzheimer’s disease. Alzheimers Dement. 2021;7:e12154. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 74. Therriault J, Pascoal TA, Savard M, Benedet AL, Chamoun M, Tissot C, et al. Topographic distribution of amyloid-β, tau, and atrophy in patients with behavioral/dysexecutive Alzheimer disease. Neurology. 2021;96:e81–92. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 75. Nisbet RM, Van der Jeugd A, Leinenga G, Evans HT, Janowicz PW, Gotz J. Combined effects of scanning ultrasound and a tau-specific single chain antibody in a tau transgenic mouse model. Brain. 2017;140:1220–30. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 76. Anglada-Huguet M, Rodrigues S, Hochgrafe K, Mandelkow E, Mandelkow EM. Inhibition of Tau aggregation with BSc3094 reduces Tau and decreases cognitive deficits in rTg4510 mice. Alzheimers Dement (N Y). 2021;7:e12170. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 77. Di J, Siddique I, Li Z, Malki G, Hornung S, Dutta S, et al. The molecular tweezer CLR01 improves behavioral deficits and reduces tau pathology in P301S-tau transgenic mice. Alzheimers Res Ther. 2021;13:6. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 78. Bossers K, Wirz KT, Meerhoff GF, Essing AH, van Dongen JW, Houba P, et al. Concerted changes in transcripts in the prefrontal cortex precede neuropathology in Alzheimer’s disease. Brain. 2010;133:3699–723. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 79. Berchtold NC, Coleman PD, Cribbs DH, Rogers J, Gillen DL, Cotman CW. Synaptic genes are extensively downregulated across multip